    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="527b5d04-b916-5c39-8935-bab20a4e9197" activityNameId="bf8e110f-0561-5b90-9856-33c420dee904" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sewer system, construction, vitrified clay pipe, DN 600, profile 3</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sewer system, construction, vitrified clay pipe, DN 600, profile 3
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 6b40b5d2-db48-4717-963c-b5ac60e0c16e
This process models 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with vitrified clay pipe and a trench depth of 3 meters. This process includes the production phase (A1–A3) and the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) for 1 meter of installed vitrified clay pipe, including trench excavation and backfilling. Disposal and deconstruction processes are excluded and modelled separately specific for each sewer system type. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 600, profile 3 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Vitrified clay pipe, ID 600 mm, outer diameter 728 mm, wall thickness 64 mm, 267 kg/m, 2000 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6b40b5d2-db48-4717-963c-b5ac60e0c16e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
